# The build context is the repository root, and almost none of it belongs in an image.
#
# bin/ and obj/ are the ones that matter rather than merely bloat: they hold Windows build output
# that would be copied over the restore the SDK stage just did inside the image, and the failure
# is a publish that mixes two platforms' artefacts rather than an error.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/
TestResults/

# Nothing in the test projects is published, and leaving them out keeps the context small.
backend/tests/

.git/
.github/
.vs/
.idea/
.claude/

# Never, under any circumstances, into an image.
.env
**/*.user

# Documentation is for the repository, not the runtime.
*.md
LICENSE

# The development database's compose file. deploy/ holds the one that matters here, and the
# Caddyfile inside it is copied explicitly by the web stage.
docker-compose.yml
